 "title": "A finite rule on knots grows the pinwheel law",
 "subject": "Whether the pinwheel's parity law can be grown by a rule with no coordinates",
 "conclusion": "Label each distinction of the pinwheel's parity law by its two knots' side types, its place along them and whether they run the same way: only eleven labels occur, and a fixed table (every knot into five, every distinction into the pieces its label names, five new distinctions per knot) regrows the law exactly at every level. No coordinate or angle enters the rule, and the only T-junctions are at midpoints of long legs.",
